.TH FROST 1 "October 2026" "FrostCenter 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
frost \- MSI laptop fan control and thermal monitoring for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frost
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-read\-only\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B FrostCenter
is a modern GTK3 application for monitoring and controlling fan curves,
temperature thresholds, and battery health on MSI laptops via direct ACPI
Embedded Controller (EC) port I/O (/dev/port).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show program version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-read\-only\fR
Start in read-only monitoring mode (no EC register writes).
.SH PRIVILEGES
Full fan curve editing and battery charge threshold modification requires
root privileges to access \fB/dev/port\fR. When launched from desktop environments,
privilege escalation is handled via PolicyKit (\fBpkexec\fR). When launched from
an interactive terminal, \fBsudo\fR is used automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/frostcenter/
Application files and motherboard definition database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.gsriram24.frostcenter.policy
PolicyKit policy granting graphical privilege escalation.
.TP
.I /etc/frostcenter/config.json
System-wide user configuration file.
.SH AUTHORS
G Sriram <gsriram2403@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR sudo (8)
